questions.question_text:
Estimate the area of this parcel of land using one application of the trapezoidal rule.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,5.6);
\coordinate (D) at (0,3.2);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$22\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick, dashed] (A) -- (D) node[midway, left] {$16\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick, dashed] (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$28\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick] plot [smooth] coordinates {(D) (1.5,4.2) (3.0,5.0) (C)};
\draw (A) rectangle ++(0.3,0.3);
\draw (B) rectangle ++(-0.3,0.3);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the estimated area of this block of land using two applications of the trapezoidal rule.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (M) at (1.6,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,3.0);
\coordinate (E) at (1.6,4.2);
\coordinate (C) at (3.2,3.6);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B);
\draw[thick, dashed] (A) -- (D) node[midway, left] {$30\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick, dashed] (M) -- (E) node[midway, left] {$42\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick, dashed] (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$36\text{ m}$};
\draw[thick] plot [smooth] coordinates {(D) (0.8,3.8) (E) (2.4,4.1) (C)};
\node[below] at (0.8,0) {$16\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (2.4,0) {$16\text{ m}$};
\draw (A) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (M) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (B) rectangle ++(-0.25,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
